{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790331440,"nonce":"RTb2C2XqkPXzsdax/Q9wtBZKm2Q=","title":"Lua: line attribution is per statement, not per token as luaK assigns it","message":"Line attribution is per statement, not luaK's per token. Operators, calls ('(' line), constructor items, `then`/`do` tests and closures (lastlinedefined) lack their own lines. The main chunk's implicit return fires no line event. sethook leaves a stale oldpc, which fires a spurious event on the caller's line. The generic-for explist line is wrong, and for-header errors have no position without debug. error()'s level is honoured only when it is a literal, and a level at a C function still gets a position.\n\nWhere the official 5.4.9 suite stops on it: db.lua:25/124-131,145-150,164-168,178-180,193-210,686; errors.lua:402-404,407-437,444,447.\n\nSubsystem: lowering (line tracking) + debug hooks. Plan root cause RC-line-model, package LO-line-model. Related: 4f04957, 5a27a50 (partial); new.","files":null}]}